{{#is_alert}}
The coordinator's read-cache refresh for `{{key.name}}` failed more than 3 times in 5 minutes on `{{env.name}}`.
A healthy refresher never emits this counter: `network_totals:<window>` refreshes every 60 s, `stats:v1` every 30 s, and `leaderboard:*` only on a cache miss.
Sustained failures mean the public stats plane is degrading — `/v1/network/totals`, `/v1/stats` or `/v1/leaderboard` will answer 503 once the last good body ages out of its 5-minute safety TTL.

Most often the cause is the 10 s store timeout on the `provider_earnings` aggregates (`coordinator/api/cache_refresher.go` logs `cache refresh failed; keeping previous value` with the error).
Check: `curl -s https://api.darkbloom.dev/v1/network/totals?window=24h`, coordinator logs for `cache refresh failed`, and `pg_stat_activity` for long-running aggregates.
Runbook: docs/operations/coordinator-deploy.md, "Alerting".
{{/is_alert}}
{{#is_recovery}}
Read-cache refresh for `{{key.name}}` on `{{env.name}}` is succeeding again.
{{/is_recovery}}
